36:26.859 --> 36:31.644
us. So is there any other questions

36:31.677 --> 36:34.726
or slides that we haven't seen or any other direction? I know we kind of

36:35.226 --> 36:36.983
cut you off in the middle. Is there anything else that you'd like to have

36:37.483 --> 36:40.063
specific questions on? No, I just wanted feedback on this, and I think I've gotten

36:40.563 --> 36:44.454
everything unless Councilmember Wood is online and He wants to add anything? He's not online

36:44.486 --> 36:48.558
to my knowledge. He said he couldn't make it. That's okay. I talked

36:49.058 --> 36:51.283
to him a little bit, but go ahead. Well, I was just going to ask,

36:51.299 --> 36:55.034
because you, you brought up the reason for this is more transparency

36:55.050 --> 36:58.448
with residents, which I agree with. I, I talked to, um,

36:58.657 --> 37:01.767
Evan. I think he's working on some things for the website to break down,

37:02.039 --> 37:05.694
because there's a lot of confusion around Meta and why did we bring

37:05.726 --> 37:09.671
them on and what are the, what are the, uh, tax tax incentives,

37:10.120 --> 37:13.428
having that out with these projects as they

37:13.928 --> 37:17.667
come through would be great, just to have that available. Whatever can be publicly

37:17.683 --> 37:21.007
made available would go a long way with residents

37:21.507 --> 37:24.475
there. But I think Evan's already— and maybe you're working on that project as well.

37:24.523 --> 37:26.819
Yeah, no, he worked on that, and that's great. It was just— I think it

37:27.319 --> 37:30.336
was more for data centers and what happened there with the incentives. We were looking

37:30.352 --> 37:34.173
just to do a framework for our targeted industries and how

37:34.189 --> 37:37.739
that could play out, because really my focus has been if we can get

37:38.239 --> 37:42.139
high-paying jobs in companies, manufacturing companies or whatever here, if we can get high-paying jobs,

37:42.717 --> 37:46.331
then the retail will follow. Everybody wants an Olive Garden or a Texas Roadhouse or

37:46.831 --> 37:49.463
something, but we have too many people that leave during the day. So how do

37:49.963 --> 37:53.494
we create the environment for jobs here locally that people stay here and

37:53.994 --> 37:56.754
spend here locally that will entice these other retail projects to come in?

37:58.232 --> 38:00.528
We definitely know there would be nothing to the west of us.

38:01.532 --> 38:04.414
all 20-something acres of that if it wasn't for some of the stuff that we

38:04.478 --> 38:08.332
brought in. I bet Lehigh once said that about west of

38:08.832 --> 38:12.009
them. Well, the point of the mountain. That was a dairy farm when I was

38:12.025 --> 38:15.782
a kid and there was nothing there. So yeah, west meaning

38:15.798 --> 38:19.090
us. Mayor, I mean, I really liked what Councilmember

38:19.590 --> 38:22.414
Hewish said because I think that, I think if we,

38:22.799 --> 38:24.967
and I don't want to create a,

38:28.010 --> 38:31.377
I'm not looking for an advertisement, let me say it that way, but I

38:31.877 --> 38:35.645
