38:40.168 --> 38:43.645
it in her comments, right? I mean, I don't think most

38:44.145 --> 38:47.774
people recognize that that first data center came in and really saved the residents from

38:48.274 --> 38:50.873
a tremendous tax increase that they were going to be looking at because there was

38:50.922 --> 38:53.706
water that had to be taken down from our contract from CUP.

38:54.813 --> 38:57.796
It had to happen. And so either the residents were going to pay for it

38:58.296 --> 39:01.341
or an industry business was going to come in and help pay for it.

39:01.405 --> 39:04.421
And Meta, in fact, did that. I don't think people realize that.

39:05.560 --> 39:09.409
And so the circumstances on the ground in 2017 or 2018 or

39:09.909 --> 39:13.034
whenever that happened were much different than they are today, just as our

39:13.534 --> 39:17.365
circumstance is different. And the residents are going to question everything we've

39:17.865 --> 39:20.253
done. In fact, they're already doing it and they'll continue to do it. And that's

39:20.753 --> 39:24.414
okay, they should. But I think context

39:24.495 --> 39:28.287
is what really matters. And I think, Evan, if you're working on that, I really

39:28.787 --> 39:32.191
would like to encourage that the complete story is out there where people can evaluate

39:32.691 --> 39:34.328
it and look at it. I don't want it to be propaganda, that's not my

39:34.376 --> 39:38.249
goal. But I would like to have the factual data so that they understand

39:38.749 --> 39:42.265
that we had an obligation on

39:42.765 --> 39:44.772
a contract to put some water to use, and we were going to pay for

39:45.272 --> 39:48.575
it whether we put it to use or not. Anyway, and electricity,

39:48.831 --> 39:52.038
they brought in that 3, that 345, 350. That's really helped out a lot.

39:52.135 --> 39:55.486
A lot of times even manufacturing plants can't do anything without that. They need

39:55.986 --> 40:00.072
like a 3-phase. I just don't think our residents really understand that. I didn't understand

40:00.572 --> 40:03.760
it until I landed here, and even being here, I still know there's things I

40:04.260 --> 40:07.271
don't know. But the more I learn, the more I go, oh well, that makes

40:07.771 --> 40:11.841
sense. Somebody made a decision that I've questioned and I've wondered about, but had

40:12.341 --> 40:15.049
I sat there at that time, I might have found yourself in exactly the same

40:15.549 --> 40:18.776
spot with all of the context. Just to give a little plug

40:18.840 --> 40:22.453
to Natalie, she does the resident engagement, the School

40:22.953 --> 40:25.842
of Correct. So, and it, it is something that I go over in that.

40:25.906 --> 40:29.568
