02:34:26.552 --> 02:34:30.019
a lot going on. So, and, and I said this before, that Turkey Trot,

02:34:30.309 --> 02:34:33.615
man, the socks— you better get there early. That's all I'm gonna say.

02:34:34.036 --> 02:34:35.797
If you want Turkey Trot socks, get there early.

02:34:37.526 --> 02:34:40.798
And then just a question I have a question on those announcements too.

02:34:41.364 --> 02:34:45.666
I'm not 100% sure, but I think that Healthy City designation

02:34:46.166 --> 02:34:49.416
might have— the trophy or plaque might be at my house.

02:34:49.706 --> 02:34:52.604
Did we have a place we want to put that here? Oh, absolutely.

02:34:52.990 --> 02:34:56.451
I'll— I can't remember. Did you remember? Did you end up with it?

02:34:56.789 --> 02:34:58.949
I think I might. I think you have it. Okay, so I need to get

02:34:59.449 --> 02:35:00.501
that over here so we can display it.

02:35:03.606 --> 02:35:06.798
Thank you. So the next one You're already ready,

02:35:06.831 --> 02:35:10.735
Natalie. This— and this is the coolest thing— is this the 3rd one

02:35:10.783 --> 02:35:14.301
we did, right? 4th one. I lose track. And I'm telling

02:35:14.317 --> 02:35:17.981
you, if you're a citizen, a resident here, and you haven't been through the academy,

02:35:18.853 --> 02:35:21.662
do it. It's awesome. All these graduates are going to tell you they learned a

02:35:22.162 --> 02:35:24.986
lot and they have a different perspective than Facebook now.

02:35:25.469 --> 02:35:27.611
So go ahead.

02:35:29.640 --> 02:35:32.652
All right, uh, we'll go ahead and invite the council to come down in front

02:35:32.716 --> 02:35:36.318
while I give a quick explanation for those who haven't heard about the Citizens Academy.

02:35:36.916 --> 02:35:40.521
It is a 6-week interactive course. You come to the city

02:35:40.779 --> 02:35:44.271
once a week for a little 2-hour course, and you get to meet with our

02:35:44.771 --> 02:35:48.720
department heads, and they explain to you what their jobs are, how the different departments

02:35:49.220 --> 02:35:52.424
of the city interact with each other. You get to see some things you wouldn't

02:35:52.924 --> 02:35:55.550
normally get to see or smell, like our sewer treatment plant.

02:35:55.856 --> 02:35:58.502
That one's always a crowd favorite. Um,

02:36:00.051 --> 02:36:03.472
and it's just a really cool opportunity to get to know the city and to

02:36:03.843 --> 02:36:06.205
also get to meet people in your community.

02:36:07.071 --> 02:36:10.982
Um, before we go ahead and dive into reading

02:36:11.079 --> 02:36:14.205
their names, I just want to say that,

02:36:15.006 --> 02:36:19.238
um, as in recognition of getting— sorry, of attending

02:36:19.286 --> 02:36:23.086
and graduating from the Eagle Mountain Academy, these participants will receive

02:36:23.182 --> 02:36:26.500
a t-shirt which is special edition. You can only get it

02:36:26.564 --> 02:36:30.797
if you attend the academy. You'll receive a certificate and

02:36:30.829 --> 02:36:34.972
a pin, because as we work together to ascend together

02:36:34.988 --> 02:36:38.006
as a community, these individuals have earned their wings.

02:36:38.360 --> 02:36:41.651
And so you will receive your wings tonight. So, um, as we

02:36:41.796 --> 02:36:45.200
call each individual, please go ahead and come on up here to

02:36:45.264 --> 02:36:49.102
receive your certificate, and feel free to shake hands down the

02:36:49.118 --> 02:36:52.570
line. And then after we read your name, feel free to

02:36:53.070 --> 02:36:55.524
just kind of stand off to the side because we'll invite you back up at

02:36:56.024 --> 02:36:58.374
the end for group picture. All right,

02:36:58.986 --> 02:37:02.723
tonight we are recognizing the following: Ashley Barrett.

02:37:17.130 --> 02:37:18.202
Tyler Bateman.

02:37:25.661 --> 02:37:26.514
Rob Burton.

02:37:33.694 --> 02:37:39.453
Tyson Ayer.

02:37:40.573 --> 02:37:41.563
Amy Hart.

02:37:47.573 --> 02:37:48.578
Katherine Jamison.

02:37:53.807 --> 02:37:54.631
Brett Jones.

02:38:00.236 --> 02:38:00.855
Evelyn Julian.

02:38:05.680 --> 02:38:06.841
Jonathan Monroe.

02:38:11.920 --> 02:38:13.258
Christine Montgomery.

02:38:18.186 --> 02:38:19.116
Bob Peterson.

02:38:24.211 --> 02:38:26.532
And last but not least, Shirley Peterson.

02:38:44.331 --> 02:38:47.940
All right, let's hear it one more time for the graduating cohort of Eagle

02:38:48.440 --> 02:38:52.458
Mountain Academy. The council,

02:38:53.200 --> 02:38:56.506
the council can go ahead and head back up, and we'll have

02:38:57.006 --> 02:38:57.861
the participants stand in front.

02:39:05.324 --> 02:39:09.323
Yep, go ahead and stand in the front. The council members will stand behind

02:39:33.704 --> 02:39:37.298
Perfect. Thank you.

02:39:38.125 --> 02:39:51.507
All right,

02:39:51.540 --> 02:39:54.644
congratulations. We appreciate you guys coming. I get to go to some of those classes

02:39:54.677 --> 02:39:57.380
towards the end. It's A little bit harder. I got too busy, but, uh,

02:39:57.685 --> 02:39:59.805
super fun getting to know everybody and participating.

02:40:00.784 --> 02:40:04.252
Um, the next item— we set aside a time—

02:40:04.752 --> 02:40:08.331
I got to slow down so I can talk. We set time aside for public

02:40:08.831 --> 02:40:13.067
comment. As a reminder, public comment is an opportunity for the community members to

02:40:13.567 --> 02:40:17.162
address the city council, and each speaker is allowed up to 3 minutes.

02:40:17.483 --> 02:40:20.437
If you wish to speak during the public comment portion,

02:40:21.180 --> 02:40:24.252
please complete a comment form in the back and

02:40:24.380 --> 02:40:27.329
bring it back to our city recorder over here on this side, to Lacey.

02:40:28.162 --> 02:40:31.831
Council members will listen but not engage in discussion during public comment.

02:40:32.392 --> 02:40:35.998
We ask that everyone remain respectful. Disruptive behavior,

02:40:36.014 --> 02:40:39.298
including cheering, booing, clapping, or comments directed

02:40:39.798 --> 02:40:43.577
at individual city employees, is prohibited. If you have issue or

02:40:43.689 --> 02:40:47.134
questions regarding staff or personnel, administrative staff will meet

02:40:47.634 --> 02:40:50.998
you in the foyer for a for further discussion. Lastly, public comment period

02:40:51.498 --> 02:40:54.895
is for items not associated with a scheduled public hearing. If your

02:40:54.927 --> 02:40:58.103
comment relates to a public hearing item, please wait until that item is called.

02:40:58.632 --> 02:41:01.968
Tonight's public hearings are on the agenda, 15A and 15B,

02:41:02.769 --> 02:41:06.458
which are land use— have to deal with

02:41:06.958 --> 02:41:11.109
the land use map and the Code 1768.85

02:41:11.609 --> 02:41:13.963
regarding artificial turf. So we'll wait for those. Thank you.

02:41:15.062 --> 02:41:18.005
Any other comments? We will start now.

02:41:18.134 --> 02:41:20.858
It is 7:15, and I will open our public comment period.

02:41:21.800 --> 02:41:22.986
Lacey. Tiffany Ulmer.

02:41:33.420 --> 02:41:36.782
Hi, Tiffany Ulmer. I recently,

02:41:37.057 --> 02:41:40.861
about a year ago, purchased a farm on Lake Mountain Road at the

02:41:41.123 --> 02:41:45.717
end of the long dirt road south of John

02:41:45.733 --> 02:41:49.259
Hancock. And recently the road

02:41:49.759 --> 02:41:53.684
conditions have become terrible. And I was trying to figure out what was causing them.

02:41:53.844 --> 02:41:57.210
I expect a dirt road to be a dirt road. I get that.

02:41:57.691 --> 02:42:01.201
But right now Lake Mountain Road is literally a lake

02:42:01.378 --> 02:42:04.952
mountain. I mean, you could probably see carp swimming in

02:42:05.048 --> 02:42:08.398
the big puddles. It's so bad, especially in front of John

02:42:08.495 --> 02:42:12.025
Hancock. And that made me wonder why we didn't have

02:42:12.058 --> 02:42:15.365
John Hancock finish building the road all the way

02:42:15.430 --> 02:42:18.982
to the edge of their property. It's only like halfway through, and that's the

02:42:18.998 --> 02:42:22.933
area that needs to be taken care of. It's muddy,

02:42:23.435 --> 02:42:27.828
it's foot-deep water, there's a

02:42:28.300 --> 02:42:31.539
water main thing that's buried that if you don't know it's there, you're going to

02:42:31.555 --> 02:42:32.678
hit it and damage your vehicle.

02:42:35.221 --> 02:42:38.568
So maybe we need to follow up with John Hancock and maybe have them

02:42:38.633 --> 02:42:42.238
finish that section of road that should belong to them,

02:42:42.351 --> 02:42:43.467
is who I'm assuming.

02:42:46.814 --> 02:42:50.213
Also, the road's getting worse because it

02:42:50.713 --> 02:42:55.100
has recently was relabeled as a

02:42:55.165 --> 02:42:57.625
construction entrance for one of the data centers.

02:42:58.365 --> 02:43:01.484
And so now we have data center traffic going down this dirt road,

02:43:01.597 --> 02:43:04.784
big vehicles. And it's really getting torn up.

02:43:04.961 --> 02:43:08.237
And the residents who've lived there before me

02:43:08.737 --> 02:43:12.092
and my farm for a year, they say that it's a lot worse

02:43:12.592 --> 02:43:16.123
than what it usually is. So if we can maybe check that out. I also

02:43:16.623 --> 02:43:19.416
reported trash such as a sofa,

02:43:20.540 --> 02:43:23.849
tires, and other things to the app. And the person

02:43:23.897 --> 02:43:27.125
on the app wrote back saying, hey, we're going to close this, but we'll take

02:43:27.625 --> 02:43:30.356
care of it. They still have yet to pick up any of the trash or

02:43:30.856 --> 02:43:34.724
that stuff. Um, it's a sofa. I can't pick up a sofa

02:43:35.224 --> 02:43:38.869
to take with me. So if we could just do something to

02:43:38.886 --> 02:43:41.545
help Lake Mountain Road out a little, I'd appreciate it.

02:43:41.982 --> 02:43:42.240
Thanks.

02:43:47.173 --> 02:43:50.391
Okay, that's it for public comment. Is there anyone here that did not have the

02:43:50.891 --> 02:43:54.605
opportunity to speak? Seeing no one, at 7:18 we'll close

02:43:55.105 --> 02:43:58.048
the public comment period and come back to the council and I'll start over here

02:43:58.080 --> 02:44:01.197
on the island with Zach. Councilmember Hughes. I'm on my own.

02:44:01.310 --> 02:44:04.860
I'm holding down the fort on this side of the dais today.

02:44:04.925 --> 02:44:08.749
Appreciate everyone coming tonight. Congratulations to those

02:44:08.781 --> 02:44:11.834
that just received their awards.

02:44:11.978 --> 02:44:15.192
We're always trying to educate residents. I've lived

02:44:15.692 --> 02:44:18.919
here over 20 years and there's a lot that I still don't know about our

02:44:19.419 --> 02:44:22.647
city. And I look at the infrastructure and all of the projects that we have

02:44:22.679 --> 02:44:27.192
going on and We get a weekly email from

02:44:27.305 --> 02:44:31.466
Ben Reeves, our city administrator, and there's usually 35,

02:44:31.660 --> 02:44:35.731
40 projects on that. I mean, it's a long email of everything

02:44:35.779 --> 02:44:39.741
we have going. I just don't think people realize what

02:44:40.241 --> 02:44:43.790
that means when you're the 9th fastest growing city in America, not just

02:44:44.290 --> 02:44:46.138
in the state of Utah, but in the United States.

02:44:47.351 --> 02:44:50.859
Is it appropriate for me to address Tiffany Ulmer's comments?

02:44:51.164 --> 02:44:54.665
You can. Is that okay? So maybe just to follow

02:44:54.778 --> 02:44:57.909
up on, on that road. I have had a couple other people

02:44:58.409 --> 02:45:01.186
reach out to me regarding the data center traffic. I don't know if they're getting

02:45:01.780 --> 02:45:05.265
routed that way or why. It doesn't seem like it'd be an efficient path to

02:45:05.330 --> 02:45:08.429
take on a dirt road with a big truck. But I also

02:45:08.526 --> 02:45:12.686
personally, I, I had an issue earlier in my park

02:45:12.702 --> 02:45:16.652
where I was reporting tree stumps where the parks

02:45:17.152 --> 02:45:20.585
department had cut the tree down because they had died, and we reported that

02:45:21.085 --> 02:45:24.727
the tree had died, but they had just cut the tree, left the stump,

02:45:24.743 --> 02:45:28.050
and we have about 5 or 6 of those in our local park. When I

02:45:28.550 --> 02:45:32.545
reported that, they similarly closed the issue and

02:45:33.045 --> 02:45:36.912
it never got resolved. And I'm wondering what the incentive structure is

02:45:37.008 --> 02:45:41.053
for those that are responding to those app requests

02:45:41.553 --> 02:45:44.859
as they come through. Why are they closing them out? I think we should probably

02:45:44.971 --> 02:45:48.231
keep them open until they're absolutely confirmed done.

02:45:48.503 --> 02:45:51.859
In my employment, we have a

02:45:52.359 --> 02:45:55.424
process that we follow. We call it a double do, where the person doing the

02:45:55.924 --> 02:45:59.647
single do, the first person at the at the job, reports that it's complete,

02:45:59.663 --> 02:46:03.244
and somebody comes back after them and confirms that it was done correctly.

02:46:03.292 --> 02:46:07.242
So I'm wondering if we can evaluate what that process

02:46:07.354 --> 02:46:10.277
looks like within the city and not just close them out because as residents,

02:46:10.341 --> 02:46:14.413
you're expecting for that. It exists to report that and to take

02:46:14.913 --> 02:46:18.241
action for the city. And if we're closing them out, they're not happening. I would

02:46:18.741 --> 02:46:21.362
just be curious if that's something that we could maybe take a second look at.

02:46:21.947 --> 02:46:25.291
And just grateful for everybody that came tonight. Thank you.

02:46:28.751 --> 02:46:30.998
Thanks, Mayor. Welcome everyone.

02:46:33.084 --> 02:46:36.407
Just wanted to report on the chili cook-off. I was going to

02:46:36.907 --> 02:46:40.756
win first place, but I didn't. Me too. So Councilmember

02:46:40.804 --> 02:46:44.074
Whiting took the first annual chili cook-off with the seniors,

02:46:44.219 --> 02:46:47.505
and he won, and Councilmember Clark took second,

02:46:47.537 --> 02:46:50.129
and I took third, and the mayor got honorable mention.

02:46:52.644 --> 02:46:55.490
But it was a lot of fun. We enjoyed it. I met the Petersons there

02:46:55.700 --> 02:46:59.000
at the chili cook-off, and I want to congratulate them. They'd only been in

02:46:59.032 --> 02:47:03.055
the city 2 weeks when they signed up to take the Citizens

02:47:03.555 --> 02:47:06.665
Academy courses. And I just, I just applaud that.

02:47:06.858 --> 02:47:09.233
I mean, they moved to a new city. They said, we want to understand what's

02:47:09.281 --> 02:47:12.721
going on and how do we get involved. And, and they, they've inserted

02:47:12.754 --> 02:47:17.303
themselves into things in the community. And I'm just grateful for people like them and

02:47:17.803 --> 02:47:18.389
to each of you that are here.

02:47:21.099 --> 02:47:24.267
And I'm grateful that Lake Powell got 14 feet of water over the course

02:47:24.767 --> 02:47:28.095
of the last week. I'm super grateful for the rain and just ask our residents

02:47:28.111 --> 02:47:31.724
to do all that you can to prepare for that extra rain. We're praying

02:47:31.822 --> 02:47:35.000
for it. We're hoping for it. And we better be prepared when it comes

02:47:35.097 --> 02:47:37.682
to divert it away from those areas we want to keep it out of.

02:47:38.612 --> 02:47:41.833
So, and I would, Tiffany, I would just, I would make

02:47:42.333 --> 02:47:45.424
one comment about John Hancock. I don't know the circumstances about that road,

02:47:45.456 --> 02:47:49.173
but my, I'm going to give you an assumption based on my experience. My assumption

02:47:49.673 --> 02:47:51.777
is, is the city probably could not compel them to do that, or we would

02:47:52.277 --> 02:47:55.690
have. And it probably belongs to someone else,

02:47:55.770 --> 02:47:59.753
or we can let staff answer that for you, but that's That's

02:47:59.817 --> 02:48:03.254
my assessment. Does staff know? Does anybody know about that that would

02:48:03.302 --> 02:48:07.362
be willing to speak to it? State law governing school,

02:48:07.571 --> 02:48:10.271
specifically governing public schools like charter schools,

02:48:11.750 --> 02:48:15.694
says that we cannot require them to dedicate road or

02:48:16.194 --> 02:48:19.664
to build it out past essentially their entrance. So in this

02:48:20.164 --> 02:48:23.585
case, where there's, unless there's certain other circumstances that aren't applicable here.

02:48:24.406 --> 02:48:28.461
So in this case, where John Hancock's just kind of out there, and it's by,

02:48:29.095 --> 02:48:31.077
you know, approved but not built subdivision,

02:48:33.017 --> 02:48:36.901
and that portion of Lake Mountain Road, they could essentially have to build it

02:48:37.401 --> 02:48:40.688
to their last entrance to the school. And we can't, even though their property line

02:48:41.188 --> 02:48:44.075
goes further, we can't compel them to build out the road any further than that.

02:48:44.867 --> 02:48:48.598
And that's just a matter of state law. Take that up with your Utah

02:48:48.679 --> 02:48:52.553
Legislative Corps group. They're the ones who can make that adjustment, and we've lobbied

02:48:53.053 --> 02:48:56.812
them to make some changes regarding the requirements for schools. Cities are very limited

02:48:57.312 --> 02:48:59.421
in what they can require schools to do, charter or public.

02:49:04.820 --> 02:49:08.217
Awesome. Thank you, Mayor. It's, it's always fun to see you guys here, and I

02:49:08.717 --> 02:49:11.866
love that you availed yourself of the Citizens Academy because it's

02:49:12.366 --> 02:49:15.828
a really cool opportunity to learn more about what goes on in our city.

02:49:16.496 --> 02:49:20.630
I wanna give some kudos to our

02:49:20.663 --> 02:49:23.690
staff. We're told through,

02:49:24.044 --> 02:49:27.602
like, the budgeting process and everything else that we need to try to

02:49:28.102 --> 02:49:31.242
do more with less. And I agree, that's what we have to do in our

02:49:31.853 --> 02:49:35.732
family budgets. And I like the

02:49:36.232 --> 02:49:39.837
creativity of finding technology to help us

02:49:40.337 --> 02:49:43.371
stretch our resources a little bit more. Thank you.

02:49:43.717 --> 02:49:47.075
And I think the ME AI is

02:49:47.123 --> 02:49:50.947
a perfect example of that because we're always trying to find enough

02:49:51.447 --> 02:49:54.787
employees to staff customer service and utility billing

02:49:54.803 --> 02:49:58.049
and try to find an employee who speaks the language

02:49:58.549 --> 02:50:02.017
of the person who's coming up and asking questions. And what's cool about this

02:50:02.050 --> 02:50:04.877
technology is for a fixed amount every year,

02:50:05.408 --> 02:50:08.862
we can have it in like 72 different languages and they can

02:50:08.878 --> 02:50:11.368
answer questions 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.

02:50:11.913 --> 02:50:15.382
And I think that this is going to be a neat way for our

02:50:15.882 --> 02:50:19.797
residents to get answers when they can't otherwise contact

02:50:19.813 --> 02:50:23.330
someone at the city. So I'm grateful that they did that, and I love that

02:50:23.830 --> 02:50:27.504
there's a text because I hate emailing, but that's a little thing about

02:50:28.004 --> 02:50:32.000
me. I also want to thank our veterans. With Veterans Day

02:50:32.500 --> 02:50:35.773
coming up, I'm so grateful for all that we have in our community all that

02:50:36.273 --> 02:50:39.620
we have in our country, and because of the people who've

02:50:40.120 --> 02:50:43.708
put everything on the line so that we can be at home safe

02:50:44.208 --> 02:50:47.539
with our families. I'm excited for the Veterans Day breakfast.

02:50:47.699 --> 02:50:50.954
That's something that the city has been doing for a really long time,

02:50:51.306 --> 02:50:54.977
and I— there's been some

02:50:55.571 --> 02:50:59.306
changes in the American Legion post recently, and our city

02:50:59.322 --> 02:51:03.317
event staff has just stepped up and didn't miss a beat. They're making

02:51:03.349 --> 02:51:07.106
sure that it comes forward and coordinating with Scouts

02:51:07.606 --> 02:51:11.297
in the community and our American Legion, what's left

02:51:11.797 --> 02:51:15.279
of it, and working to make sure that we still do a really cool veterans

02:51:15.311 --> 02:51:19.164
breakfast. So if you know someone in your neighborhood, please invite

02:51:19.664 --> 02:51:23.339
them to come to that. It's, it's for them and their families, and we really

02:51:23.839 --> 02:51:26.438
want to make sure that they have that opportunity to be honored by our community.

02:51:27.838 --> 02:51:31.349
Last week, some of us on City Council with our staff and

02:51:31.381 --> 02:51:35.522
our mayor got to go for what some people call a retreat or

02:51:36.022 --> 02:51:39.390
conference, but I call it a really long meeting, at the Utah League of

02:51:39.890 --> 02:51:43.707
Cities and Towns on Tuesday and Wednesday. And you start your day like at

02:51:44.207 --> 02:51:47.575
7 in the morning up at the Salt Palace, and you go until like 4:30,

02:51:47.591 --> 02:51:51.074
5 o'clock at night. And all day long there's classes,

02:51:51.892 --> 02:51:56.177
and there's classes so that our recorder's office can get certifications,

02:51:56.726 --> 02:51:59.978
And our communications

02:52:00.074 --> 02:52:03.779
team can see what's going on and learn from other

02:52:04.279 --> 02:52:07.868
comms teams in the city world. And it

02:52:08.368 --> 02:52:12.005
was a really great experience to go up there and to connect with other cities,

02:52:12.919 --> 02:52:16.399
to connect with some of our state leaders, and just

02:52:16.752 --> 02:52:19.943
to learn more about how to do this job better for you guys.

02:52:21.081 --> 02:52:24.322
