02:56:36.693 --> 02:56:40.720
Uh, we're receiving, uh, MAG funding for that project.

02:56:41.025 --> 02:56:43.800
Um, so this agreement is the golf course,

02:56:44.634 --> 02:56:48.749
uh, essentially giving us the land in exchange as payment

02:56:49.249 --> 02:56:53.349
for debts that it already owes the city. And so it's approximately,

02:56:53.413 --> 02:56:57.253
I think, if memory serves, about 3.5 acres of land in various spots

02:56:57.543 --> 02:57:00.835
that we need as part of the Ranches Parkway widening project.

02:57:03.312 --> 02:57:06.865
The debts that they owe us relate to the initial purchase

02:57:07.365 --> 02:57:10.806
of the, of the golf course from the city. For those

02:57:10.920 --> 02:57:15.261
who may be unfamiliar with the history of that, the golf course was originally owned

02:57:15.309 --> 02:57:19.075
by the original developer of the ranches. It was then later sold

02:57:20.056 --> 02:57:23.724
to the city or given to the city, and the city then later

02:57:24.255 --> 02:57:27.055
